Manual end-to-end probe of the built server (dist/index.js), #471.
Fixture repo: /tmp/cez-471-probe with a seeded .ai/cezar/todos.json holding one entry.

==================== DEFAULT (no CEZ_FOLLOWUPS) ====================
$ CEZ_DRY_RUN=1 node dist/index.js --repo /tmp/cez-471-probe -p 4499 --no-open

GET /api/health  -> capabilities: {'localHandoff': False, 'followups': False}
GET /api/todos   -> []                       # the seeded entry is hidden
DELETE /api/todos/seeded-1
                 -> HTTP 409 {"error":"the follow-up inbox is disabled — set CEZ_FOLLOWUPS=1 to enable it"}
todos.json on disk after all of the above:
  [{"id":"seeded-1","ts":"2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"a pre-existing follow-up","runnable":false}]
  # hidden, NOT destroyed — the whole point of the gate

==================== CEZ_FOLLOWUPS=1 ====================
$ CEZ_DRY_RUN=1 CEZ_FOLLOWUPS=1 node dist/index.js --repo /tmp/cez-471-probe -p 4498 --no-open

GET /api/health  -> capabilities: {'localHandoff': False, 'followups': True}
GET /api/todos   -> [{"id":"seeded-1","ts":"2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"a pre-existing follow-up","runnable":false}]
                    # back verbatim: the round trip off -> on loses nothing
DELETE /api/todos/seeded-1
                 -> HTTP 200 {"removed":true}
todos.json on disk -> []                     # enabled behavior unchanged

(localHandoff:False is unrelated to this change — the probe binds outside loopback.)
